## Writing for readers

{{#if view.coordinator}}
- A write-up others will read is a separate document from the internal staging record; draft it from the staging document once its findings are settled.
- Before presenting it: `provenance` (new, {{owner}}'s prior work, or classical?), `expositor` (can a peer learn from it?), a fidelity check against the staging document, then `cold-reader` (can a stranger follow it?). Order: the `gate-chain` skill.
- Name the intended reader in each reviewer's brief.
- The rules and {{owner}}'s model text: [docs/discipline/exposition.md](docs/discipline/exposition.md).
{{/if}}
